Title: THE LAST FERRY
Author: Lin Park
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:


EXT. MIST HARBOR - DAWN

MIRA ASH ties a BRASS COMPASS to her belt. PILOT GARRON counts fares.
GARRON
Last crossing till the moon turns.

EXT. NEAR SHORE VILLAGE - MORNING

Mira passes a boy, ELI, 10, selling river charms.
ELI
Take me across someday. I want to see the lantern city.
MIRA
Not till you can pay without losing what keeps you kind.

INT. FERRY - DAY

Passengers board. A WOLF-HOODED STRANGER offers a silver thimble.
STRANGER
Lists lag behind the dead.

EXT. RIVER MIDCHANNEL - DAY

The water blackens. Shapes swim beneath the hull.
GARRON
The river tests what you refuse to release.

INT. FERRY - DAY

Mira's iron compass spins toward the stranger.
MIRA
You paid with a brass coin, not a fare. And you're not on the manifest.

INT. FERRY HOLD - DAY

Mira finds a crate marked ASH — inside, river charms like the ones Eli, barely seven, carved by the dock.
MIRA
Someone's been paying fares with other people's keepsakes.

EXT. RIVER MIDCHANNEL - DAY

Garron rings the bell three times. Fog thickens into walls.
GARRON
Choose your memory before the river chooses for you.

INT. FERRY - DAY

Mira holds a memory orb — Eli laughing. The stranger reaches.
MIRA
I pay my own fare. Always.

EXT. FAR SHORE - DUSK

Lantern towers rise. Passengers disembark, dazed, lighter.
GARRON
Some arrive. Some become the toll.

EXT. FAR SHORE DOCK - DUSK

The stranger lowers her hood — OLDER MIRA. The compass points back across the water, toward Eli's village.
OLDER MIRA
Next time, don't leave the boy on the near bank.

FADE OUT.


THE END
